# Canonical acceptance specification for DT-05 (#24), M2.
# Source criteria: the GitHub story intake at
# https://github.com/anthonygraca/gherkin-knowledge-graph/issues/24 (verified 2026-11-13T13:05Z)
# and roadmap §7 (M2). Failure and boundary scenarios were added during refinement; the two intake
# scenarios keep their intent. Executed by the Cucumber suite (bdd/) from M2 onward.
@DT-05 @issue-24 @M2
Feature: DT-05: Test outcomes associated with exact tested commits
  Verification evidence is append-only. Each run names the commit that was executed; the commit that
  merely stores the report is never substituted for it. Freshness decisions compare content hashes,
  so an evidence-only commit cannot look like a source change.

  @SCN-2001
  Scenario: Evidence records the revision that was executed
    Given a test run for "TEST-002" executed at the "baseline-b-change" revision
    When the evidence is read
    Then it carries the commit SHA that was executed, not the commit that stored the record
    And it records the result, the execution time, and the run URI

  @SCN-2002
  Scenario: Several runs of one test are kept
    Given "TEST-002" passed at "baseline-a" and failed at "baseline-b"
    Then both records exist with distinct evidence ids
    And the later run does not overwrite the earlier one

  @SCN-2003
  Scenario: An evidence-only commit changes no artifact content hash
    Given the fixture baselines "baseline-a" and "baseline-b"
    When the artifact content hashes are compared across the evidence-only commit
    Then no artifact is reported as changed
    And the evidence still identifies the source commit it tested

  @SCN-2004
  Scenario: Evidence naming an unknown test is rejected
    Given a repository revision whose evidence references unknown test artifact "TEST-999"
    When the revision is ingested
    Then ingestion fails with an error naming "TEST-999"
# Canonical acceptance specification for DT-06 (#25), M2.
# Source criteria: the GitHub story intake at
# https://github.com/anthonygraca/gherkin-knowledge-graph/issues/25 (verified 2026-11-13T13:05Z)
# and roadmap §7 (M2). Executed by the Cucumber suite (bdd/) from M2 onward.
@DT-06 @issue-25 @M2
Feature: DT-06: Changed artifacts and impacted accepted links between baselines
  Change detection is content-hash based, not commit-SHA based, and belongs to the repository port.
  The assurance rules consume the change set; they do not re-implement the diff.

  @SCN-2011
  Scenario: Change set between baseline-a and baseline-b
    Given the fixture repository with both baselines ingested
    When the change set between them is requested
    Then the changed artifacts are exactly "CODE-001" and "TEST-002"
    And "TEST-001" is reported unchanged
    And an evidence-only commit does not mark artifacts as changed

  @SCN-2012
  Scenario: Impacted accepted links
    Given "CODE-001" changed between the two baselines
    When impacted links are requested
    Then the accepted links reaching "CODE-001" are reported
    And links to unchanged artifacts are not

  @SCN-2013
  Scenario: The change set identifies artifacts added at the later baseline
    Given an artifact exists at "baseline-b" but not at "baseline-a"
    When the change set between them is requested
    Then the added artifact is reported as changed
# Canonical acceptance specification for AS-02 (#3), M2.
# Source criteria: the GitHub story intake at
# https://github.com/anthonygraca/gherkin-knowledge-graph/issues/3 (verified 2026-11-13T13:05Z)
# and its task children #5/#6. Executed by the Cucumber suite (bdd/) from M2 onward.
@AS-02 @issue-3 @M2
Feature: AS-02: Potential stale-evidence findings after relevant changes
  A passing run whose relevant content changed afterwards requests reverification. It is never a
  verification failure: no recorded execution failed.

  @SCN-2021
  Scenario: Implementation changed since verification
    Given "SCN-001" verifies "REQ-001"
    And a test for "SCN-001" passed at baseline "baseline-a" with evidence "EV-001"
    And a relevant linked implementation changed at baseline "baseline-b"
    And no later matching verification evidence exists
    When assurance evaluates baseline "baseline-b"
    Then a "reverification_required" finding is produced for "REQ-001"
    And the finding identifies both baselines and the changed artifact "CODE-001"
    And "REQ-001" is not marked "verification_failed"

  @SCN-2022
  Scenario: Unchanged content needs no reverification
    Given a test for "SCN-001" passed at baseline "baseline-a" with evidence "EV-001"
    And no relevant artifact changed at baseline "baseline-a"
    When assurance evaluates baseline "baseline-a"
    Then no "reverification_required" finding names "REQ-001"

  @SCN-2023
  Scenario: A later run replaces the freshness decision, not the history
    Given "TEST-002" passed at "baseline-a" and failed at "baseline-b"
    When assurance evaluates baseline "baseline-b"
    Then the failing evidence "EV-003" produces a "verification_failed" finding
    And the earlier passing evidence "EV-002" is still recorded
# Canonical acceptance specification for AS-03 (#4), M2.
# Source criteria: the GitHub story intake at
# https://github.com/anthonygraca/gherkin-knowledge-graph/issues/4 (verified 2026-11-13T13:05Z)
# and roadmap §4/§7. Executed by the Cucumber suite (bdd/) from M2 onward.
@AS-03 @issue-4 @M2
Feature: AS-03: Keep failed, missing, and potentially stale evidence distinct
  One evaluation can contain all three situations. Their meanings are different and their
  precedence is declared: a confirmed failure at the evaluated baseline wins for its scenario;
  a stale pass is a request for reverification; a missing accepted link is a coverage gap.

  Rule: The distinctions are visible in one evaluation

    @SCN-2031
    Scenario: Distinguish missing, failed, and stale evidence in one evaluation
      Given "REQ-001" has passing verification evidence at baseline "baseline-a"
      And "REQ-002" has no accepted verification scenario
      And "REQ-003" has a failing test at baseline "baseline-b"
      And a relevant linked implementation of "REQ-001" changed at baseline "baseline-b"
      When assurance evaluates baseline "baseline-b"
      Then "REQ-002" yields a "missing_verification_link" finding
      And "REQ-003" yields a "verification_failed" finding
      And "REQ-001" yields a "reverification_required" finding
      And no finding downgrades "reverification_required" to "verification_failed"

  Rule: Applicability is decided by content, not commit identity

    @SCN-2032
    Scenario: Evidence recorded at a source commit applies to its evidence commit
      Given evidence "EV-001" was recorded at the source commit of "baseline-a"
      And the evidence commit stores the report without changing artifact content
      When assurance evaluates baseline "baseline-a"
      Then the evidence is treated as applicable
      And "REQ-001" has no "verification_failed" finding
