@AS-02 @issue-3 @M2
Feature: AS-02: Potential stale-evidence findings after relevant changes
  A passing run whose relevant content changed afterwards requests reverification. It is never a
  verification failure: no recorded execution failed.

  @SCN-2021
  Scenario: Implementation changed since verification
    Given "SCN-001" verifies "REQ-001"
    And a test for "SCN-001" passed at baseline "baseline-a" with evidence "EV-001"
    And a relevant linked implementation changed at baseline "baseline-b"
    And no later matching verification evidence exists
    When assurance evaluates baseline "baseline-b"
    Then a "reverification_required" finding is produced for "REQ-001"
    And the finding identifies both baselines and the changed artifact "CODE-001"
    And "REQ-001" is not marked "verification_failed"

  @SCN-2022
  Scenario: Unchanged content needs no reverification
    Given a test for "SCN-001" passed at baseline "baseline-a" with evidence "EV-001"
    And no relevant artifact changed at baseline "baseline-a"
    When assurance evaluates baseline "baseline-a"
    Then no "reverification_required" finding names "REQ-001"

  @SCN-2023
  Scenario: A later run replaces the freshness decision, not the history
    Given "TEST-002" passed at "baseline-a" and failed at "baseline-b"
    When assurance evaluates baseline "baseline-b"
    Then the failing evidence "EV-003" produces a "verification_failed" finding
    And the earlier passing evidence "EV-002" is still recorded
# Canonical acceptance specification for AS-03 (#4), M2.
# Source criteria: the GitHub story intake at
# https://github.com/anthonygraca/gherkin-knowledge-graph/issues/4 (verified 2026-11-13T13:05Z)
# and roadmap §4/§7. Executed by the Cucumber suite (bdd/) from M2 onward.
@AS-03 @issue-4 @M2
Feature: AS-03: Keep failed, missing, and potentially stale evidence distinct
  One evaluation can contain all three situations. Their meanings are different and their
  precedence is declared: a confirmed failure at the evaluated baseline wins for its scenario;
  a stale pass is a request for reverification; a missing accepted link is a coverage gap.

  Rule: The distinctions are visible in one evaluation

    @SCN-2031
    Scenario: Distinguish missing, failed, and stale evidence in one evaluation
      Given "REQ-001" has passing verification evidence at baseline "baseline-a"
      And "REQ-002" has no accepted verification scenario
      And "REQ-003" has a failing test at baseline "baseline-b"
      And a relevant linked implementation of "REQ-001" changed at baseline "baseline-b"
      When assurance evaluates baseline "baseline-b"
      Then "REQ-002" yields a "missing_verification_link" finding
      And "REQ-003" yields a "verification_failed" finding
      And "REQ-001" yields a "reverification_required" finding
      And no finding downgrades "reverification_required" to "verification_failed"

  Rule: Applicability is decided by content, not commit identity

    @SCN-2032
    Scenario: Evidence recorded at a source commit applies to its evidence commit
      Given evidence "EV-001" was recorded at the source commit of "baseline-a"
      And the evidence commit stores the report without changing artifact content
      When assurance evaluates baseline "baseline-a"
      Then the evidence is treated as applicable
      And "REQ-001" has no "verification_failed" finding
# Canonical acceptance specification for AS-05 (#27), M2.
# Source criteria: the GitHub story intake at
# https://github.com/anthonygraca/gherkin-knowledge-graph/issues/27 (verified 2026-11-13T13:05Z)
# and roadmap §7 (M2). Dashboard behaviour is verified by Vitest component tests and a recorded
# browser demonstration; browser-level Cucumber execution is tracked in the GT-02 inventory.
@AS-05 @issue-27 @M2 @ui-component
# Executable-status note: Findings drill-down rendering is verified by Vitest component tests and a recorded browser demonstration; browser-level Cucumber bindings are pending under GT-02.
Feature: AS-05: Drill-down into findings and their evidence
  The dashboard must let a reviewer judge whether a finding is justified: which rule fired, at which
  baseline, on which artifacts, with which evidence and tested commit. Reverification and confirmed
  failure must remain differentiable by wording, not only by colour.

  @SCN-2041
  Scenario: Drill into a reverification finding
    Given the "reverification_required" finding for "REQ-001" at "baseline-b"
    When the finding is opened in the dashboard
    Then it names the rule, the evaluated baseline, and the changed artifact
    And it shows the evidence "EV-001" with the revision it was executed at
    And it does not present the requirement as failed

  @SCN-2042
  Scenario: A confirmed failure is presented differently
    Given the "verification_failed" finding for "REQ-003" at "baseline-b"
    When the finding is opened
    Then the failing evidence "EV-003" and its revision are shown
    And the wording states a failed verification, not a reverification request
